Third-party components
----------------------
KitePlayer decodes media through KiteFFmpeg (https://github.com/yuroyami/KiteFFmpeg),
a separate Apache-2.0 project, consumed as a dependency and not vendored into
this repository. KiteFFmpeg in turn links against FFmpeg's libav* libraries
(https://ffmpeg.org), licensed under the LGPL-2.1-or-later (or the GPL when
built with --enable-gpl). FFmpeg is NOT covered by this NOTICE or by
KitePlayer's Apache-2.0 license, and neither is KiteFFmpeg's own NOTICE.

Depending on the FFmpeg build flavour a consumer links, the linked FFmpeg may
additionally bundle third-party codec and rendering libraries (SVT-AV1,
libvpx, libaom, libopus, libmp3lame, libwebp, FreeType, HarfBuzz, FriBidi,
libass, x264/x265 in the GPL flavour, and others), each under its own
license. The complete component list, per-component licenses, and the
distribution obligations they carry are documented at:
https://yuroyami.github.io/KiteFFmpeg/licensing/
(source: docs/licensing.md in the KiteFFmpeg repository).

kiteplayer-libass links, statically, into its published artifacts:
libass 0.17.4 (ISC, https://github.com/libass/libass), HarfBuzz 14.2.1 (MIT,
https://github.com/harfbuzz/harfbuzz), FreeType 2.14.3 (FreeType License,
https://freetype.org) and FriBidi 1.0.16 (LGPL-2.1-or-later,
https://github.com/fribidi/fribidi). Their license texts ship inside the
artifacts under META-INF/licenses/kiteplayer-libass/. FriBidi's LGPL terms
apply to those artifacts; its source is the tagged upstream release, and the
archives are built by KiteFFmpeg's buildAssChainFor* tasks and published as
release assets of that repository.
